       {
        "title": "Growth Compensation",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p><strong>Balancing Correction “Various Weights”:</strong><br/>Correction of unbalance by adding or removing weights (e.g., balancing screws). Includes the option to specify existing weight sets.</p> <p><strong>Balancing Correction “Shift</strong><br/><strong>Weights”:</strong> Compensates for unbalance by rotating balancing rings or slotted nuts.</p> <p><strong>Balancing “Radial</strong><br/><strong>Drilling”:</strong> <strong>Provides correction</strong> for unbalance through radial drilling. Automatically calculates the number, angular position, and depth of the drill holes.</p> <p><strong>Balancing correction “Milling</strong><br/><strong>”:</strong> Compensates for unbalance through radial, tangential, or axial milling.</p> <p><strong>Balancing correction “Axial</strong><br/><strong>Drilling”:</strong> Compensates for unbalance through axial drilling. Automatic calculation of the number, angular position, and depth of the drill holes.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1097",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
